# N3 example: variable-predicate-dependency.
# Companion to variable-predicate-dependency.srl: an intentional
# negative cycle (derived depends on not blocked; blocked depends on
# derived), expressed with fixed predicate names the way
# is (the variable-predicate aspect is SPARQL-RL specific; the cycle is
# the point of the test either way).
#
# unstratifiable, N3 has no stratification analysis; its deferred
# log:notIncludes mechanism instead derives BOTH :Derived and :Blocked --
# checking that :Blocked did not hold yet at the point it deferred, then
# firing :Derived, only for the second (ordinary, non-negated) rule to
# add :Blocked immediately afterward, retroactively invalidating the
# premise :Derived relied on. This is exactly the kind of unsound result
# stratification exists to rule out.

@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#>.
@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyepl/examples/variable-predicate-dependency#>.

:a :source :blocked.

{?x :source :blocked. ?SCOPE log:notIncludes {?x a :Blocked}.} => {?x a :Derived}.
{?x a :Derived} => {?x a :Blocked}.
